  "source_dataset": "CADECV2",
  "text": "Significant weight gain.\nChronic constipation.\nMajor loss of libido.\nWanting to sleep all the time.\nNo energy.\n\"\nZoning out\" feeling every day for hours at a time.\nSweating.\nIntense craving for sweets.\nNot giving a care for anything or anyone.\nNo emotions.\nHowever it DID work great for the depression.\nI weaned off this med after taking it for 6 years because I felt my life situation was better and I didn't need it anymore.\nI took the last dose 6 weeks ago\nand I am still having major withdrawal symptoms of dizziness, irritability, loose stools, crazy \"zapping\" feeling that goes thru my head, ringing in my ears, headaches, blurry vision and stomach cramps.\nI had a feeling of my heart racing and high blood pressure at first but that has went away.\nIt did work great great for my depression, however,  I would only recommend this drug to someone who is so depressed they are suicidal due to the extreme side-effects coming off of it.\nThe side-effects are very unpleasant and last for a very long time.\n",
